                <pb facs="0223" n="209" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg209"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">839.154/12–1644: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in the Dominican Republic</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Briggs</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-12-21T21:00:00-04:00">December 21,
                            1944—9 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>441. Authorization requested in your telegrams 533 and 534 of December 16 is
                    granted. Public Roads states that none of the $65,000 should be used by
                    Dominicans to purchase additional equipment, since sufficient equipment for
                    completion of road has long been available to them, and that expense of any such
                    equipment should be met by Dominican Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
